WEBVTT

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:05.640
Present Day

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.590
Present Time

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:23.340
And you don't seem to understand

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:28.540
A shame you seemed an honest man

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:33.290
And all the fears you hold so dear

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:38.560
Will turn to whisper in your ear

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:41.960
And you know what they say might hurt you

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:44.430
And you know that it means so much

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:49.190
And you don't even feel a thing

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:54.850
I am falling, I am fading

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:58.970
I have lost it all

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:26.990
I am falling, I am fading, I am drowning

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.630
Help me to breathe

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:34.840
I am hurting, I have lost it all

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:37.380
I am losing

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:41.580
Help me to breathe

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:16.230
If you can hear it, it is speaking to you.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:22.400
And if you can see it, then it is your...

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:35.080
Mankind is a creature that no longer evolves, is it not?

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:40.290
Compared to other animals, the cancer rate in man is exceedingly small.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:45.730
One theory says that man is a neoteny, and is no longer able to evolve.

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:52.270
If this is true, then what an absurd creature man has evolved into.

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:56.770
Not knowing what it is that drives them,

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:01.280
they keep their bodies merely to satisfy the desires of the flesh.

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.710
They're worthless, don't you think?

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.150
That's all mankind is.

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:19.260
But it is no longer necessary to remain a wretched human being.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:25.560
Mankind has finally created an exit whereby he may escape.

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:28.880
What do you mean?

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:33.540
The network. The Wired, Lain.

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:36.650
Who are you?

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:40.110
I am God.

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:58.860
Wanna go get something to eat?

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:01.340
Hey, aren't you hungry?

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:09.670
Hey, wanna go to the pool next time?

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:31.660
Oh, man...

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:57.140
Tell me a story!

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:15.140
Come on, please!

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:22.150
Tell me a story, okay?

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:26.210
What kind of story would you like to hear, Lain?

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:28.220
Let's see...

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.220
Something I don't know about!

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:41.540
There is nothing that you don't know.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:45.230
I can't tell you a story that doesn't exist.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:48.110
You understand, don't you?

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.890
Well, how about this, then?

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:57.480
For every event, there is first a prophecy.

00:05:57.970 --> 00:06:01.960
An event first comes into existence when there is a prophecy.

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:05.960
Who? Who makes the prophecies?

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:16.040
Throughout Tokyo today, the VTCZX road traffic information transmission system

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:17.850
sent out incorrect information.

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:23.580
Especially at congested intersections, traffic signals interfered with the

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:27.860
auto-drive program in cars and trucks, sending them out of control.

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:32.120
There was a fatality in Shibuya, Tokyo,

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:35.460
but the Information Ministry says that the system is already back up,

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:37.870
and that such an accident will never happen again.

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:20.160
Excuse me.

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:21.240
Huh?

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:23.030
Uh...

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:29.670
Mind if I hit on you?

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:40.390
Oh, shit...

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:41.450
Later!

00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:44.060
H-Hey!

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:49.760
That little creep...

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:56.200
Damn it, this is gonna stain...

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:05.560
The other side is overcrowded. The dead will have no place to go.

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:08.940
W-What the heck is this?

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:15.020
Some kind of bad joke?

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:20.760
What the hell?

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:22.070
What's she doing?

00:08:22.070 --> 00:08:23.660
Is she crazy?

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:42.350
Lain?

00:08:44.970 --> 00:08:47.580
What's her problem?

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:31.250
The prophecy is being fulfilled, Lain.

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:35.310
But then it's not a prophecy.

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:37.440
No, it is a prophecy.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:41.950
History is not merely a linear collection of points that

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:45.890
we pass through on a timeline.

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:48.750
They are connected by a line.

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:53.770
No, perhaps it is more accurate to say that they are made to connect.

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:58.400
By who? Who connects them?

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:23.930
Lain!

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:32.460
What did you do?

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:37.370
I had no idea. I guess you're pretty good.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:41.400
I didn't know you could pull off a hacking stunt like that already.

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:43.360
What're you talking about?

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:45.400
Playing innocent again, huh?

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:48.480
I really don't...

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:51.010
You didn't do it, Lain?

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:53.460
Do what?

00:10:57.240 --> 00:11:00.430
The Information Control Bureau of the Information Ministry

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:03.330
began investigating yesterday's information network abnormality,

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:06.420
stating that it was very likely a deliberate act.

00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:11.830
With the network now a lifeline for not only the city, but for society,

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:15.480
such an act is tantamount to...

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:32.240
Your total is 948 yen.

00:11:32.510 --> 00:11:35.090
Out of 948 yen. Please, enjoy your meal.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:38.500
Huh? There it is again.

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:39.990
Again?

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:41.500
What?

00:11:41.500 --> 00:11:43.870
Spam. Indiscriminate mail.

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:45.470
I'm really getting tired of this...

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:47.910
"Fulfill the prophecy," right?

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:51.010
Is it a declaration of war by some cult group?

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:56.870
I asked some geeks I met on the Wired about it a while ago.

00:11:56.870 --> 00:11:59.620
They said it might be the Knights.

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:01.810
Knights? Who's that?

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:05.490
Some kind of super-hacker group.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:09.450
But I thought hackers don't usually work together.

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:15.330
True. But maybe this Knights group really isn't a group at all.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:21.610
They say they have a lot of power in the Wired, and that they do a lot in secret.

00:12:21.610 --> 00:12:23.970
So they're a secret society.

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:27.770
Geez, do they get their kicks out of this stuff?

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:30.480
I'm not sure why...

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:31.470
Huh?

00:12:32.870 --> 00:12:37.480
...but something tells me that they're not in it for fun or for money.

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:58.830
It's reasonable to see the Wired as an upper layer of the real world.

00:12:58.830 --> 00:13:03.250
In other words, physical reality is nothing but a hologram

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:05.840
of the information that flows through the Wired.

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:08.840
Mom?

00:13:08.840 --> 00:13:12.790
This is because the body, the activity of the human brain, is merely

00:13:12.790 --> 00:13:19.420
a physical phenomenon caused by synapses delivering electrical impulses.

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:22.310
I...

00:13:22.310 --> 00:13:28.860
The body exists only to verify one's own existence.

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:33.950
Are you... Are you really my mom?

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:40.550
Are you?

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:17.830
Lain?

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:20.330
Huh?

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:24.790
Didn't I see you at Shibuya?

00:14:33.290 --> 00:14:35.680
Forget it. It's nothing.

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:45.840
Thank you!

00:15:46.930 --> 00:15:49.740
Hey, don't you think he's pretty cute?

00:15:56.170 --> 00:15:58.460
How did it go with him?

00:15:58.460 --> 00:16:00.510
Come on, you can tell us!

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:32.940
Fulfill the prophecy!

00:16:35.710 --> 00:16:38.320
W-What? What prophecy?!

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:16.400
What's going on?

00:17:16.400 --> 00:17:19.100
I usually have dinner with Mom and Dad about now...

00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:22.360
Wha...

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:28.040
What's happening?

00:17:40.640 --> 00:17:43.560
I-Is someone there?

00:17:51.120 --> 00:17:54.210
Come on, I know you're there.

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:29.390
Fulfill the prophecy!

00:18:45.340 --> 00:18:48.390
Are you my real dad?

00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:54.940
It may be that what flows through the Wired isn't merely electrical information.

00:18:55.310 --> 00:18:56.400
Huh?

00:18:56.700 --> 00:19:00.410
If we assume that it was the development of electricity and phones

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:02.470
that brought about the formation of the Wired,

00:19:02.470 --> 00:19:08.670
then I have to wonder if another world was created at that moment.

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:10.410
Uh...

00:19:10.410 --> 00:19:15.420
Here in the real world, God exists only as a concept.

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:20.420
But in the Wired, there may be a sort of Deus-like embodiment.

00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:22.290
God?

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:27.230
I don't know whether or not it should be called a god.

00:19:27.230 --> 00:19:29.760
But at the very least, I think it has the same kind

00:19:29.760 --> 00:19:33.310
of power that is written of in myths.

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:37.940
I think I may have talked with God.

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:42.850
It's possible that the Deus of the Wired may already have enough power

00:19:42.850 --> 00:19:46.910
to affect the real world in some instances.

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:50.380
Yes... In the form of prophecy.

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:55.180
Prophecy?

00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:06.060
What's wrong?

00:21:06.060 --> 00:21:09.570
It's nothing. Forget about it.

00:22:08.870 --> 00:22:11.590
Who is it today?

00:22:29.570 --> 00:22:34.000
nan no tsumi mo nai hazu na no ni

00:22:29.570 --> 00:22:34.000
Although I must be innocent,

00:22:34.000 --> 00:22:37.910
nanraka no batsu wo uketeru

00:22:34.000 --> 00:22:37.910
now I am punished.

00:22:38.340 --> 00:22:44.210
jibun de maita tane de mo nai no ni

00:22:38.340 --> 00:22:44.210
I wasn't the one who sowed those seeds, but nevertheless

00:22:44.930 --> 00:22:51.120
sakimidareta hana tsumasareru

00:22:44.930 --> 00:22:51.120
I have to pull up the flowers that bloomed from them.

00:22:57.670 --> 00:23:02.310
shiranai koto to mo ienai ga

00:22:57.670 --> 00:23:02.310
I can't say I didn't know about it,

00:23:02.310 --> 00:23:06.760
katabou katsuida oboe wa nai

00:23:02.310 --> 00:23:06.760
but I don't remember taking any part in it.

00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:12.950
jiyuu wo takaku kawasareta ki mo suru ga

00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:12.950
I think my freedom cost me dearly,

00:23:13.480 --> 00:23:20.190
kokoro made yasuku utta oboe wa nai

00:23:13.480 --> 00:23:20.190
but I don't remember selling my soul so cheaply.

00:23:20.550 --> 00:23:28.240
Hey Hey kutabatte osaraba suru made

00:23:20.550 --> 00:23:28.240
Hey hey, until I die and say farewell...

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:38.150
Hey Hey dare no te ni mo kakaranai

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:38.150
Hey hey... no one can touch me.

00:23:39.670 --> 00:23:43.760
tooi yoru wo urotsuiteiru

00:23:39.670 --> 00:23:43.760
You probably don't know

00:23:43.760 --> 00:23:51.470
shiranai darou eien no narazu monotachi wo

00:23:43.760 --> 00:23:51.470
the eternal outlaws prowling in the distant night.
